IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cp4-nouns`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, section 57 -- THE DEATH BENEFIT.
--
-- A death benefit is a lump sum paid to the estate or succession of a deceased contributor
-- (paragraph 44(1)(c), piece cp3). Section 57 says how much. The amount turns on the date of death:
-- before 2019 the lesser of six times the contributor's retirement pension (worked out under
-- subsection (2)) and ten per cent of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, but never more than
-- $2,500 after 1997; $2,500 for a death after 2018; and $5,000 for a death after 2024 where the four
-- conditions of subsection (1.2) are met.
--
-- Out of range, taken as plain inputs (NOTES.md, "Cross-references out of my ranges"): the Year's
-- Maximum Pensionable Earnings (s 18, piece cp1); the retirement pension payable for the month of death
-- and the contributor's total pensionable earnings, contributory period and basic number of
-- contributory months (ss 42, 46 to 53, piece cp3); the Pension Index (s 43, piece cp3); whether a
-- death benefit or a survivor's pension is payable (s 44, piece cp3).

§ `Section 57 -- amount of death benefit`

§§ `The facts about the deceased contributor`

-- The facts about the deceased contributor that subsections (2) and (3) read. Each is a fact or an
-- amount that another section works out.
DECLARE `cp4 Deceased contributor` HAS
    `cp4 the day the contributor died` IS A DATE
    `cp4 a retirement pension was payable to the contributor for the month in which the contributor died` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cp4 the retirement pension payable to the contributor for the month in which the contributor died` IS A NUMBER
    `cp4 the contributor's contributory period ended before January 1976` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cp4 the contributor's basic number of contributory months` IS A NUMBER
    `cp4 the number of months in the contributor's contributory period` IS A NUMBER
    `cp4 the contributor's total pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER
    `cp4 the Pension Index for the year that includes the month in which the contributor died` IS A NUMBER
    `cp4 the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor's retirement pension first became payable` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Section 57(1) -- the lump sum`

-- src:1684 | 57 (1) A death benefit payable to the estate or succession of a contributor is a lump sum amount equal to
@ref Act s 57(1) (src:1684)
GIVEN contributor IS A `cp4 Deceased contributor`
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor died` IS A NUMBER
      `a death benefit is payable to the contributor's estate or succession under paragraph 44(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor has received a retirement pension or a disability pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a survivor's pension is payable under paragraph 44(1)(d) as a result of the contributor's death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 57(1) — the amount of the death benefit` contributor `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor died` `a death benefit is payable to the contributor's estate or succession under paragraph 44(1)(c)` `the contributor has received a retirement pension or a disability pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` `a survivor's pension is payable under paragraph 44(1)(d) as a result of the contributor's death` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 57(1.2) — the additional amount of $5,000 applies` (contributor's `cp4 the day the contributor died`) `a death benefit is payable to the contributor's estate or succession under paragraph 44(1)(c)` `the contributor has received a retirement pension or a disability pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` `a survivor's pension is payable under paragraph 44(1)(d) as a result of the contributor's death`
            THEN JUST 5000
        IF contributor's `cp4 the day the contributor died` AT LEAST (YMD 2019 1 1)
            THEN `s 57(1)(b) — the lump sum for a death after 2018` (contributor's `cp4 the day the contributor died`)
        OTHERWISE `s 57(1.1) — the lump sum of paragraph (1)(a) after the cap` (contributor's `cp4 the day the contributor died`) (`s 57(1)(a) — the lump sum for a death before 2019` contributor `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor died`)


-- src:1684 | 57 (1) A death benefit payable to the estate or succession of a contributor is a lump sum amount equal to
-- src:1685 | (a) if the contributor’s death occurs before January 1, 2019, the lesser of
-- src:1686 | (i) six times the amount of the contributor’s retirement pension, calculated as provided in subsection (2), and
-- src:1687 | (ii) ten per cent of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor died; or
-- src:1688 | (b) if the contributor’s death occurs after December 31, 2018, $2,500.
@ref Act s 57(1)(a) (src:1685-1687)
GIVEN contributor IS A `cp4 Deceased contributor`
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor died` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 57(1)(a) — the lump sum for a death before 2019` contributor `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor died` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 57(2) — the retirement pension used for paragraph (1)(a)` contributor
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST pension THEN JUST (min (6 TIMES pension) (10% TIMES `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor died`))

-- src:1688 | (b) if the contributor’s death occurs after December 31, 2018, $2,500.
@ref Act s 57(1)(b) (src:1688)
GIVEN `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 57(1)(b) — the lump sum for a death after 2018` `the day the contributor died` MEANS
    IF `the day the contributor died` AT LEAST (YMD 2019 1 1)
    THEN JUST 2500
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1690 | (1.1) Despite paragraph 57(1)(a), when the contributor’s death occurs after December 31, 1997, the lump sum referred to in that paragraph shall not exceed $2,500.
@ref Act s 57(1.1) (src:1690)
GIVEN `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE
      `the lump sum referred to in paragraph (1)(a)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 57(1.1) — the lump sum of paragraph (1)(a) after the cap` `the day the contributor died` `the lump sum referred to in paragraph (1)(a)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the lump sum referred to in paragraph (1)(a)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST lumpSum THEN
        IF `the day the contributor died` AT LEAST (YMD 1998 1 1)
        THEN JUST (min lumpSum 2500)
        ELSE JUST lumpSum

-- src:1692 | (1.2) Despite subsection (1), a death benefit payable to the estate or succession of a contributor is a lump sum amount equal to $5,000 if
-- src:1693 | (a) the contributor’s death occurs after December 31, 2024;
-- src:1694 | (b) a death benefit is payable to the contributor’s estate or succession under paragraph 44(1)(c);
-- src:1695 | (c) the contributor has not received a retirement pension or a disability pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan; and
-- src:1696 | (d) no survivor’s pension is payable under paragraph 44(1)(d) as a result of the contributor’s death.
@ref Act s 57(1.2) (src:1692-1696)
GIVEN `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE
      `a death benefit is payable to the contributor's estate or succession under paragraph 44(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor has received a retirement pension or a disability pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a survivor's pension is payable under paragraph 44(1)(d) as a result of the contributor's death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57(1.2) — the additional amount of $5,000 applies` `the day the contributor died` `a death benefit is payable to the contributor's estate or succession under paragraph 44(1)(c)` `the contributor has received a retirement pension or a disability pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` `a survivor's pension is payable under paragraph 44(1)(d) as a result of the contributor's death` MEANS
        `the day the contributor died` AT LEAST (YMD 2025 1 1)
    AND `a death benefit is payable to the contributor's estate or succession under paragraph 44(1)(c)`
    AND (NOT `the contributor has received a retirement pension or a disability pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan`)
    AND (NOT `a survivor's pension is payable under paragraph 44(1)(d) as a result of the contributor's death`)

§§ `Section 57(2) -- the contributor's retirement pension used in paragraph (1)(a)`

-- src:1697 | Calculation of contributor’s retirement pension
-- src:1698 | (2) The amount of the contributor’s retirement pension to be used for the purposes of paragraph (1)(a) is
@ref Act s 57(2) (src:1697-1698)
GIVEN contributor IS A `cp4 Deceased contributor`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 57(2) — the retirement pension used for paragraph (1)(a)` contributor MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (contributor's `cp4 the day the contributor died` LESS THAN (YMD 1987 1 1)) AND contributor's `cp4 a retirement pension was payable to the contributor for the month in which the contributor died`
            THEN `s 57(2)(a) — the retirement pension used for a death before 1987 when a retirement pension was payable` contributor
        IF contributor's `cp4 the day the contributor died` LESS THAN (YMD 1987 1 1)
            THEN `s 57(2)(b) — the retirement pension used for a death before 1987 when none was payable` contributor
        IF NOT (contributor's `cp4 a retirement pension was payable to the contributor for the month in which the contributor died`)
            THEN JUST (`s 57(2)(c)(i) — the retirement pension used for a death after 1986 when none was payable` contributor)
        OTHERWISE `s 57(2)(c)(ii) — the retirement pension used for a death after 1986 when one was payable` contributor

-- src:1699 | (a) in the case of a contributor who died before January 1, 1987 and to whom a retirement pension was payable for the month in which he died, the amount of such pension for that month, but where that contributor’s contributory period ended before January 1976, the amount is the amount of the retirement pension payable for the month in which he died multiplied by the ratio that the basic number of contributory months bears to the number of months in the contributor’s contributory period;
@ref Act s 57(2)(a) (src:1699)
GIVEN contributor IS A `cp4 Deceased contributor`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 57(2)(a) — the retirement pension used for a death before 1987 when a retirement pension was payable` contributor MEANS
    IF contributor's `cp4 the contributor's contributory period ended before January 1976`
    THEN
        IF contributor's `cp4 the number of months in the contributor's contributory period` EQUALS 0
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (contributor's `cp4 the retirement pension payable to the contributor for the month in which the contributor died` TIMES ((contributor's `cp4 the contributor's basic number of contributory months`) DIVIDED BY (contributor's `cp4 the number of months in the contributor's contributory period`)))
    ELSE JUST (contributor's `cp4 the retirement pension payable to the contributor for the month in which the contributor died`)


-- src:1700 | (b) in the case of a contributor who died before January 1, 1987 and to whom no retirement pension was payable for the month in which he died, an amount equal to twenty-five per cent of his average monthly pensionable earnings, calculated as provided in sections 46 to 53 except that, in making that calculation,
-- src:1701 | (i) subsections 46(3) to (6) and section 47 are not applicable,
-- src:1702 | (ii) subsection 48(1) shall be read as follows:
-- src:1703 | “48(1)Subject to subsections (2), (3) and (4), the average monthly pensionable earnings of a contributor are an amount calculated by dividing his total pensionable earnings by the total number of months in his contributory period.”, and
-- src:1704 | (iii) section 51 shall be read as though for the reference therein to the year in which a benefit becomes payable to the contributor there were substituted a reference to the year in which the contributor died; and
@ref Act s 57(2)(b) (src:1700-1704)
GIVEN contributor IS A `cp4 Deceased contributor`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 57(2)(b) — the retirement pension used for a death before 1987 when none was payable` contributor MEANS
    -- Subparagraph (ii) reads subsection 48(1) as total pensionable earnings divided by the months in the
    -- contributory period. Subparagraphs (i) and (iii) change how sections 46, 47 and 51 are applied, in
    -- piece cp3: the two inputs below are the values that calculation gives.
    IF contributor's `cp4 the number of months in the contributor's contributory period` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (25% TIMES ((contributor's `cp4 the contributor's total pensionable earnings`) DIVIDED BY (contributor's `cp4 the number of months in the contributor's contributory period`)))

-- src:1704 | (iii) section 51 shall be read as though for the reference therein to the year in which a benefit becomes payable to the contributor there were substituted a reference to the year in which the contributor died; and
@ref Act s 57(2)(b)(iii) (src:1704)
GIVEN `the year in which the contributor died` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 57(2)(b)(iii) — the year to which section 51 refers for a death before 1987` `the year in which the contributor died` MEANS
    `the year in which the contributor died`

-- src:1706 | (i) where a retirement pension was not payable for the month in which the contributor died, an amount equal to twenty-five per cent of his average monthly pensionable earnings, calculated as provided in subsection (3), or
@ref Act s 57(2)(c)(i) (src:1706)
GIVEN contributor IS A `cp4 Deceased contributor`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 57(2)(c)(i) — the retirement pension used for a death after 1986 when none was payable` contributor MEANS
    25% TIMES (`s 57(3) — the average monthly pensionable earnings of a contributor who died after 1986` contributor)

-- src:1707 | (ii) where a retirement pension was payable for the month in which the contributor died, the product obtained by multiplying
-- src:1708 | (A) an amount equal to twenty-five per cent of his average monthly pensionable earnings, calculated as provided in subsection (3),
-- src:1709 | by
-- src:1710 | (B) the ratio that the Pension Index for the year that includes that month bears to the Pension Index for the year in which the retirement pension first became payable, calculated, where the year in which the retirement pension first became payable was prior to 1974, as if the Pension Index for that year had not been subject to the limitation referred to in paragraph 43.1(2)(a) of the Canada Pension Plan, chapter C-5 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, of 1.02 times the Pension Index for the preceding year.
@ref Act s 57(2)(c)(ii) (src:1707-1710)
GIVEN contributor IS A `cp4 Deceased contributor`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 57(2)(c)(ii) — the retirement pension used for a death after 1986 when one was payable` contributor MEANS
    -- "that month" in (B) is the month in which the contributor died (NOTES.md, fork register, F-g).
    -- Where the year the pension first became payable is before 1974, the Pension Index supplied for that
    -- year is the one calculated without the 1.02 limitation the text names.
    IF contributor's `cp4 the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor's retirement pension first became payable` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST ((25% TIMES (`s 57(3) — the average monthly pensionable earnings of a contributor who died after 1986` contributor)) TIMES ((contributor's `cp4 the Pension Index for the year that includes the month in which the contributor died`) DIVIDED BY (contributor's `cp4 the Pension Index for the year in which the contributor's retirement pension first became payable`)))

§§ `Section 57(3) -- the average monthly pensionable earnings`

-- src:1712 | (3) Subject to subsections 48(2), (3) and (4), the average monthly pensionable earnings of a contributor is an amount calculated by dividing his total pensionable earnings by the total number of months in his contributory period or by thirty-six, whichever is greater, and
-- src:1713 | (a) in the case of a contributor to whom a retirement pension was payable for the month in which he died, section 51 applies; or
-- src:1714 | (b) in the case of a contributor to whom no retirement pension was payable for the month in which he died, section 51 applies but the reference therein to the year in which a benefit becomes payable to the contributor shall be read as a reference to the year in which the contributor died.
@ref Act s 57(3) (src:1712-1714)
GIVEN contributor IS A `cp4 Deceased contributor`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 57(3) — the average monthly pensionable earnings of a contributor who died after 1986` contributor MEANS
    -- Subject to subsections 48(2), (3) and (4) (piece cp3): the earnings and the months are taken after
    -- any deduction those subsections allow.
    (contributor's `cp4 the contributor's total pensionable earnings`) DIVIDED BY (max (contributor's `cp4 the number of months in the contributor's contributory period`) 36)

-- src:1713 | (a) in the case of a contributor to whom a retirement pension was payable for the month in which he died, section 51 applies; or
-- src:1714 | (b) in the case of a contributor to whom no retirement pension was payable for the month in which he died, section 51 applies but the reference therein to the year in which a benefit becomes payable to the contributor shall be read as a reference to the year in which the contributor died.
@ref Act s 57(3)(a), (b) (src:1713-1714)
GIVEN `a retirement pension was payable for the month in which the contributor died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the year in which a benefit becomes payable to the contributor` IS A NUMBER
      `the year in which the contributor died` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 57(3) — the year to which section 51 refers for a death after 1986` `a retirement pension was payable for the month in which the contributor died` `the year in which a benefit becomes payable to the contributor` `the year in which the contributor died` MEANS
    IF `a retirement pension was payable for the month in which the contributor died`
    THEN `the year in which a benefit becomes payable to the contributor`
    ELSE `the year in which the contributor died`
